Assistant: I see the issue now. The OptionComponent is meant to be used as part of a react-select component, not standalone. We need to wrap it in a Select component and provide the necessary context. Let's fix the preview file:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/OptionComponent-b921da27.tsx">
<change>
<description>Wrap OptionComponent in a Select component with proper context</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import Select from '@calcom/ui/components/form/select/Select';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    option: {
      type: "dropdown",
      value: "option1",
      options: ["option1", "option2", "option3"],
      label: "Select Option",
    },
    isMulti: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Multi Select",
    },
    isSelected: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Selected",
    },
    needsTeamsUpgrade: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Needs Teams Upgrade",
    },
  });

  const options = state.option.options.map(opt => ({
    label: opt,
    value: opt,
    needsTeamsUpgrade: state.needsTeamsUpgrade.value
  }));

  return (
    <Select
      options={options}
      value={options.find(opt => opt.value === state.option.value)}
      isMulti={state.isMulti.value}
      onChange={(newValue) => {
        setState(prev => ({
          ...prev,
          option: {
            ...prev.option,
            value: newValue ? (Array.isArray(newValue) ? newValue[0]?.value : newValue.value) : ''
          }
        }));
      }}
    />
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made the following changes:

1. Removed the direct usage of OptionComponent since it's an internal component of react-select
2. Imported the Select component from Cal.com's UI library instead
3. Created proper options array with the required format
4. Added proper value handling and onChange handler
5. Wrapped everything in the Select component which provides the necessary context and styling

This should resolve the "getStyles is not a function" error because now the Option component is being rendered within the proper Select context that provides all the necessary styling functions and props.

The Select component will internally use the OptionComponent we saw in the original file, but now with all the proper context and styling infrastructure in place.

